conference hold false-positive: browser main-process cmdline retains zoom.us/j/ join URL from launch forever (until browser restart), so hold_during_conference holds ALL TTS with chime-only beeps long after the meeting ended. Seen 2026-08-10: Brave launched 1d11h earlier with join URL; stale zoom client also lingered. Suggest: ignore boot-time argv URLs (age-gate cmdline matches), require live AV stream from the matched process, and/or cap via conference_max_hold_s with audible/logged hint. Also: hark doctor should surface 'conference hold ACTIVE (matched: ...)' so operators see why TTS is silent.

Verified 2026-10-26: empty successful audio inventory still promotes stale process/URL to conference active. Decision: with check_audio enabled require live audio corroboration; preserve explicit process-only mode. Playback lane also fixes concrete shared sounddevice convenience playback race for B176/B179/B180 via per-call streams and bounded owned cleanup; historical native crash attribution requires evidence before closure.